Source: device-xiaomi-diting
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: ubuntu-diting local build <ubuntu-diting@localhost>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: device-xiaomi-diting
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, initramfs-tools, mkbootimg, device-tree-compiler, iproute2, python3,
 python3-gi, alsa-utils
Recommends: linux-image-7.2.10-diting, fastrpc-diting, hexagonrpcd-diting, firmware-xiaomi-diting, modemmanager
Description: Xiaomi 12T Pro / Redmi K50 Ultra (diting) device support
 Device integration for running Ubuntu on the Xiaomi Diting (SM8475):
  - diting-mkbootimg: builds Android boot v4 boot.img/vendor_boot.img from
    the installed kernel, initramfs and DTB into /boot/diting (never flashes)
  - kernel postinst and initramfs post-update hooks calling it
  - initramfs-tools configuration and an opt-in USB debug mode
  - a USB gadget service (NCM network + ACM serial)
  - an APT pin that keeps Ubuntu's generic kernel from being installed
  - voice call audio: diting-voice-call starts the AudioReach voice graphs
    while ModemManager has a call; diting-audiopd runs the ADSP audio PD
    (adsprpcd, fastrpc-diting) for the call's echo/noise cancellation
    (topology and DSP modules from the local firmware-xiaomi-diting)
  - sensors: diting-sensors runs hexagonrpcd (hexagonrpcd-diting) for the
    sensor DSP when it comes up
 .
 Experimental, local bring-up package.
